---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  page="publications"
  title="Florent Tariolle - Publications"
  description="Publications by Florent Tariolle in adversarial machine learning and efficient learning systems."
>
  <section class="page-section page-section--standalone page-section--flush publication-list" aria-labelledby="publications-title">
    <h1 class="sr-only" id="publications-title">Publications</h1>
    <article class="publication-card listing-card" data-reveal>
      <div class="publication-meta">
        <span>CAp 2026</span>
        <span>Poster</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Opportunistic Target Selection</h2>
      <p>
        Black-box attacks that minimize only ground-truth confidence can make diffuse progress without committing to a specific adversarial class. Opportunistic Target Selection first lets an attack explore in untargeted mode, then switches to a targeted objective against the leading non-true class.
      </p>
      <p>
        Across three score-based attacks and five ImageNet classifiers, OTS improves drift-prone random-search attacks by up to 27 percentage points in success rate and reduces censored-mean iterations by 43% on ResNet-50.
      </p>
      <p class="publication-citation">F. Tariolle and F. Yger. Accepted at CAp 2026 (Conférence sur l’Apprentissage automatique).</p>
      <div class="publication-links">
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.25663" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">arXiv ↗</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Tariolle/opportunistic-target-selection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Code ↗</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Tariolle/opportunistic-target-selection/blob/main/poster/poster_beamer.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Poster ↗</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
